  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/slot_dxf_outline.cl` is regenerated.\n- `crates/app/tests/slot_dxf_sketch.rs`: `a_slot_outline_seeds_the_slot_and_cuts_it_to_size` gets two new asserts.\n- `docs/decisions/3278-slot-dxf-golden.md` records the decision.\n\nNo generator code changes.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe post-merge gate is red on `a_slot_outline_seeds_the_slot_and_cuts_it_to_size` from 6cd4f3e01 (the merge of #3136) on.\n\n- Run 44977365067 on 5bc0b7129 (#3158): green.\n- Run 44977387120 on 6cd4f3e01 (#3136): red on this one test.\n- Runs on 60c0f48bf, 24da8ad7e and bf7e68b14: red on this one test only.\n\nThe branch of #3136 did not contain #2920. Thus #3136 regenerated `slot_wide_channel_rows` but not `slot_dxf_outline.cl`.\n\nThe assert was the golden compare, `crates/app/tests/common/mod.rs:253`: `golden ...slot_dxf_outline.cl is stale; regenerate with WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test`. The asserts before it passed on main: the ends (45, 25) and (75, 25), the width 10 mm, and the cut box 42..78 x 22..28.\n\n## Readings: the golden diff\n\nThe slot has R 5 ends and the tool is 4 mm, so the cutter centre is h = 3 mm off the axis.\n\n- The header changes from `HSMW-CL v1 ... moves=9` to `HSMW-CL v2 ... moves=15`. The v2 header comes from the arc moves.\n- The 9 old moves do not change: the approach, the plunge, and the three rows at d = -3, 0 and 3 with their joins.\n- 6 moves are added after the last row, at (75, 28). They are the #2906 wall lap:\n  - `Feed` to (45, 28): the +n side.\n  - `Arc` to (42, 25) and `Arc` to (45, 22), CCW about (45, 25): the round end at a.\n  - `Feed` to (75, 22): the -n side.\n  - `Arc` to (78, 25) and `Arc` to (75, 28), CCW about (75, 25): the round end at b.\n- Each lap point is 3.000 mm from its arc centre, or 3.000 mm off the axis on a side. The lap cuts the wall to size and stays in the outline.\n- The old golden pinned rows that touch each round end only at their end points, with chord joins across the end. That left up to h (1 - cos 45 deg) = 0.88 mm of material on each end. The old shape was the wrong one.\n\n`WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test slot_dxf_sketch -- --exact a_slot_outline_seeds_the_slot_and_cuts_it_to_size` wrote the golden: the test's own path, with no hand edit. A run without `WRITE_GOLDEN` then passed against it.\n\n`trochoid_slot_dxf_outline.cl` does not change: `git diff origin/main` on it is empty, and `a_trochoidal_slot_reads_the_same_outline` passes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`a_slot_outline_seeds_the_slot_and_cuts_it_to_size` has two new asserts:\n\n- Each round end has an arc move about its arc centre, with both end points on the 3 mm cutter-centre circle.\n- No cutting move leaves the outline at the tool radius. Each end point of each cutting move is at most 3 mm (+1 um) off the axis (45, 25) -> (75, 25). Each arc turns about an axis end, at a radius of at most 3 mm. The cutter-centre stadium is convex, so a line between two points in it stays in it.\n\nThe stock-simulation assert `gouge_cells == 0` was hidden behind the stale golden. It now runs again and passes.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate test a_slot_outline_seeds_the_slot_and_cuts_it_to_size --crate camcraft-app --binary slot_dxf_sketch --exact` on origin/main 5c8340b81: FAIL. This reproduced the stale golden.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on 4c11e92b7 without the outline-containment assert: 690 steps, 0 failed, 68 min. The diff touches a `.cl` golden, so the plan maps it to all cl, post and app suites. This includes the #3136 pins in `operations`, `clearance_in_stock` and `example_catalog`.\n- On the final head (test-only and docs changes after the quick gate): `camcraft-app` `slot_dxf_sketch` 4/4, `slot_caps` 4/4, `slot_extension` 5/5, `slot_picks` 8/8 and `slot_pick_refusals` 3/3. `camcraft-motion` `slot_round_ends` 3/3 (#3136) and `machining2d` 68/68.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test slot_dxf_sketch -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --dry-run`: 205 steps. The `.cl` golden maps to every app heavy lane. The count is more than 60, so the heavy lanes were not run. The diff changes no generator code, and `slot_dxf_sketch` has no ignored tests.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes (see above).\n- The quick gate was not run a second time on the final head. The only later changes are the containment assert in `slot_dxf_sketch.rs` and the decision file. The touched binary ran on the final head.\n\nChangelog: none (test golden only; the behaviour shipped with #3136)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3278\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
